From f04e37713d31bc95caadfe6005a214cc6415b702 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noktoborus <noktoborus@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:00:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iio: adc: axp20x_adc: name the IIO device when the device
 tree matched it

axp20x_probe() took the name of the IIO device from
platform_get_device_id(pdev). That is set only when the platform id
table matched the device. When the device tree matched it (a node with
compatible "x-powers,axp221-adc", as in the overlays of the uConsole),
it is NULL, the name is NULL, and the IIO device has no file "name": a
tool that looks for "axp22x-adc" does not find it.

The driver is a cell of the AXP MFD only, and the MFD names its platform
device by the cell: "axp22x-adc", the same name the id table matches.
Take that name in both cases.
---
 drivers/iio/adc/axp20x_adc.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/adc/axp20x_adc.c b/drivers/iio/adc/axp20x_adc.c
index d9016fe1aca..066ec4722ab 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/adc/axp20x_adc.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/axp20x_adc.c
@@ -1118,7 +1118,11 @@ static int axp20x_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		info->data = device_get_match_data(dev);
 	}
 
-	indio_dev->name = platform_get_device_id(pdev)->name;
+	/*
+	 * The name of the MFD cell: platform_get_device_id() is NULL when the
+	 * device tree matched the device, and the IIO device had no name.
+	 */
+	indio_dev->name = pdev->name;
 	indio_dev->info = info->data->iio_info;
 	indio_dev->num_channels = info->data->num_channels;
 	indio_dev->channels = info->data->channels;
-- 
